WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.520
There's a lot you may not know about Australian
hunk Chris Hemsworth from before he caught

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.259
his big break as Thor, Marvel's God of Thunder.

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:11.180
From scrapping with his brothers to starring
on an Australian soap opera, here's what we

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.700
dug up about the hammer-wielding Avenger before
he took Hollywood by storm.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.890
Fashion forward

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.640
Given his rugged Hollywood image, it's somewhat
surprising that as a young kid, Hemsworth

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.609
had a knack for, well, sewing.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:28.419
"For some reason, cross-stitch was one that
I enjoyed."

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:32.860
He told W Magazine, "I think it's because
I couldn't afford any cool clothes, so I was

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.480
like, 'I'm gonna make them myself.'"

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.340
Hemsworth's interest in sewing faded when
he tried unsuccessfully to make his own pants,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.240
but the experience set him on the path to
his future career.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.240
He went on to explain,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.540
"I had a different idea every week of what
I wanted to do professionally.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.270
I'd see movies and be inspired by things."

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.780
"I guess that's why acting fits, because I
get to pretend to be all those things with

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.310
no great amount of risk or effort."

00:00:58.310 --> 00:00:59.860
Sibling rivalry

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.900
Hemsworth has fond memories of growing up
with two brothers — even if their childhood

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.819
antics sound more like Fight Club than a Hallmark
movie.

00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:10.859
On The Graham Norton Show, Hemsworth's brother
Liam recalled the two of them fighting when

00:01:10.859 --> 00:01:11.859
they were kids.

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:15.580
"Our childhood rivalry was a bit vicious — a
bit like The Hunger Games"

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.650
He wasn't joking.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:20.619
Apparently, during a fight in their kitchen,
Liam threw a knife at Chris's head.

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:21.979
"The handle hit him in the head"

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:22.979
"OH!

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:23.979
The handle side go him!"

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:28.193
"Yea, it was a warning, it was like, if you
mess with me, I'll throw a knife at your head."

00:01:28.193 --> 00:01:29.479
A soap star

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:33.539
Though Chris and Liam found success in Hollywood,
it was actually their oldest brother, Luke,

00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:35.959
who found stardom first — in Australia.

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:41.039
After landing a role on the soap opera Neighbours
in 2001, Luke quickly grew disillusioned with

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:45.649
acting and started his own flooring business
where his younger brothers often worked.

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:50.279
In 2004, Chris followed in Luke's footsteps
and landed a role on the popular soap opera

00:01:50.279 --> 00:01:55.359
Home and Away, which led to "heartthrob status"
down under — not to mention winning industry

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:55.960
awards.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.740
Dancing down under

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.459
While starring on Home and Away, Hemsworth
competed on Dancing With The Stars Australia

00:02:02.459 --> 00:02:05.299
in 2006 — and lasted seven weeks.

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:08.229
It's a tidbit from his past that he doesn't
normally bring up.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.030
But during an appearance on The Tonight Show,
Jay Leno surprised him with a clip from his

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.750
dancing competition days.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:17.100
The audience applauded wildly, but Hemsworth
assured them,

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.440
"That ended my dancing career."

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:20.470
Captain Kirk's dad

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:25.950
In 2007, Hemsworth left Home and Away — and
Australia — to pursue an acting career in

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:26.950
Hollywood.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.830
Before long, he made his big-screen debut
in the 2009 reboot of Star Trek, playing Captain

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.560
Kirk's doomed father in an intensely emotional
opening scene.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.750
Despite that fast break, Hemsworth almost
quit acting and moved back to Australia after

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.750
Star Trek.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.720
He was turning heads, but the roles weren't
exactly pouring in.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.280
"I was ready to pack it in and come home.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.920
It was like, 'This is killing me.'"

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.010
Work begets work

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:54.040
After a nine month dry spell, Hemsworth landed
a role in Cabin in the Woods, a horror movie

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.980
produced by Joss Whedon, the Buffy the Vampire
Slayer creator who would later go on to direct

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.420
Marvel's The Avengers.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:05.120
Cabin didn't see the light of day until 2012,
but it helped Hemsworth make an important

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.120
connection.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.030
It was Whedon, along with Cabin in the Woods
director Drew Goddard, who encouraged him

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:14.760
to re-audition for the title role in Thor,
after he'd already auditioned once and been

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:15.760
rejected.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.200
"Both of them were looking at the trades at
this sort of top five guys for Thor and saying,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.550
'Why aren't you in the mix here?

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.550
What happened?'

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.550
I said, 'I don't know.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:23.160
I blew my audition, I guess.'"

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.680
After a supportive phone call from Whedon
to Thor director Kenneth Branagh, Hemsworth

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.060
was back in the mix.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.570
And the rest was history.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.400
"I'm glad you know this."

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.400
"Know what?"

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.560
"I know that…"

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.500
"Know what?"

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.760
(laughs)

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.240
Superhero strength

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.400
After landing the coveted role of the God
of Thunder, Hemsworth started preparing for

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.120
the role and quickly realized he needed to
get bigger.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.280
He told the Los Angeles Times, "They kept
saying 'Yeah, get as big as you can, as big

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:51.280
as you can."

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.250
Months later, when he returned for a final
camera test, he put on his costume and went

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.790
numb within a couple minutes.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:01.390
His costume was altered, but the director
still told him to cut back on his thickness.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:05.610
"Ken said, it's good you know. You've got the size there. You should pull it back just a little bit.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:09.180
It's just sorta blocky."

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.240
Hemsworth switched up his workout program
to include more cardio and less heavy lifting

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.030
— though you wouldn't know it from watching
the movie.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.600
"It's a good look."

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.660
A Red remake

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:25.450
In 2012, a year after the success of Thor,
Hemsworth appeared in a remake of the 1980s

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:26.620
classic Red Dawn.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:31.270
With a Rotten Tomatoes score of just 13 percent,
the movie wasn't exactly a hit.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.700
It also seemed like an odd follow-up film
for Hemsworth — and that's because it really

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:36.700
wasn't.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.180
During the dry spell after Star Trek, Hemsworth
landed Red Dawn in the same week he got the

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.650
title role in Thor.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:46.139
And like Cabin in the Woods, the movie was
actually shot before his Marvel days.

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:49.380
Regarding the delay in his earlier films,
Hemsworth told MTV,

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.230
"During shooting, I didn't have any clue there
would be problems.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:55.920
And then afterwards, I heard there was a holdup
and they were having some delays, and now

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.990
it's kind of a Benjamin Button thing.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.720
As my films come out, I get younger and less
experienced."

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.480
"It's like it upsets me now."

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:06.880
Thanks for watching!

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.600
